  "verdict": {
    "outcome": "O6",
    "direction": "too-uncertain",
    "magnitude": "n/a",
    "time_horizon": "n/a",
    "confidence": "low",
    "plain": "Whether taking utilities into public ownership helps or harms the environment hinges mainly on whether it speeds up or delays the shift away from fossil fuels \u2014 and credible independent analysts genuinely disagree on that. The near-term disruption of a huge restructuring could slow decarbonisation investment even if the long-term intention is to accelerate it.",
    "biggest_unknown": "Whether public ownership of energy companies would accelerate or cause 'a hiatus in progress towards decarbonisation' \u2014 the IFS and sector bodies warn of the latter, while proponents claim the former, and no real-world UK precedent resolves it.",
    "claims": [
      {
        "tier": "stated",
        "claim": "The policy would immediately bring water companies and the Big 5 retail energy companies into public ownership.",
        "evidence_id": "M",
        "quote": "Immediately bring railways, water companies, and the Big 5 retail energy companies back into public ownership through public investment, to serve the public rather than shareholders."
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "The IFS warned that large-scale nationalisation could lead to 'years of disruption' and a hiatus in progress towards decarbonisation in the energy sector.",
        "evidence_id": "E7",
        "quote": "The IFS warned that such a large-scale nationalisation could lead to \"years of disruption\" and potentially \"a hiatus in progress towards decarbonisation in the energy sector.\""
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "The IFS warning on decarbonisation disruption was echoed by the Energy Networks Association and Renewable UK.",
        "evidence_id": "E37",
        "quote": "a concern echoed by the Energy Networks Association and Renewable UK."
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "Conversely, proponents argue nationalisation would accelerate the transition to a low-carbon economy.",
        "evidence_id": "E38",
        "quote": "nationalisation would *accelerate* the transition to a sustainable, low-carbon economy."
      },
      {
        "tier": "projected",
        "claim": "The overall impact on decarbonisation is genuinely contested, with credible voices on both sides.",
        "evidence_id": "E45",
        "quote": "While some argue nationalisation could streamline and accelerate the net-zero transition, others warn of potential disruption and delays during the restructuring process."
      },
      {
        "tier": "measurable",
        "claim": "Water companies' financial resilience is poor, with 10 out of 17 below 'standard', suggesting underinvestment under current private ownership.",
        "evidence_id": "E18",
        "quote": "10 out of 17 companies were below 'standard' for resilience, with three in the \"action required\" category."
      },
      {
        "tier": "measurable",
        "claim": "Water companies paid out \u00a32.5 billion in dividends over two years, money that was not reinvested in infrastructure.",
        "evidence_id": "E19",
        "quote": "Water companies reportedly paid out \u00a32.5 billion in dividends over two years."
      },
